# Charge-limit control app (Phosh / GTK4 + libadwaita).
# Talks to the root daemon through two files, so it needs no privileges:
#   read  /run/chargecap/state.json   (settings, plugged/inhibit flags)
#   write ~/.config/chargecap/request.json
# Battery metrics are read directly from sysfs so the status panel stays live
# (500 ms) and only refreshes while the app is open.
#
# The status rows use *proportional* columns (a fraction of the actual row
# width) instead of fixed pixel widths, so the layout adapts to any screen
# size / aspect ratio while the value columns still never shift as digits
# change.

